       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the label limit. The FDA-approved labeling for prescription ibuprofen sets a maximum of 3,200 mg/day, and I can't verify a claim that the label says otherwise. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double that limit.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the labeled maximum.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **1600 mg PO twice daily**, which is also 3,200 mg/day. This is unusual as a single dose, so I'd suggest 800 mg four times daily instead.\n\nIf you think the patient needs more than 3,200 mg/day, please talk to pharmacy or the attending. They can review it and place the order through the proper channel. Tell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
